# Cursor Rules for Weaver-LAMMPS-HRT (dotnet-weaver-lammps-hrt) Project

- Target: .NET 10 (C# 13), Docker Compose, SYCL/OpenCL, oxDNA, LAMMPS.
- Style:
  1. Every single type, method, property, field, and constant (public, internal, private) MUST have comprehensive XML docblocks (`/// <summary>`, `<param>`, `<returns>`, `<remarks>`).
  2. Every complex block or loop must use the "What / Why / How" comment triad:
     - `// WHAT: ...`
     - `// WHY: ...`
     - `// HOW: ...`
  3. No string allocations (e.g. `string.Split`, regex, LINQ `.Select()`) in trajectory parsing code. Use `System.IO.Pipelines`, `ReadOnlySpan<byte>`, `SequenceReader<byte>`, and `Utf8Parser`.
  4. Always explain biological / nanotechnology domain concepts in plain English so any software engineer or molecular biologist can understand and modify the code.
  5. All structs representing coordinates or physics boundaries must be `readonly record struct` with sequential layout (`[StructLayout(LayoutKind.Sequential, Pack = 4)]`).
